# `F.prototype = { set slot(v) { kept.push(v); } }`: what the constructor stores under `slot` is handed to the setter, which keeps it, and the object gets no property.
# The closure of the setter is in sight, so F and its layout stay: what the constructor stores flows into the setter, out of the list that keeps it, and the string that is stored there is in `handed`.
# If the store landed in the object, `slot` would be proven filled, and `handed` of Q a number while the setter has kept the object and a string is stored there.
# G, whose literal lists a method alone, and R are the control. Each field has a name of its own, so no check goes by the number of a layout.
# -- source: main.js
